---
// Destination: src/pages/privacy.astro
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Enterprise Agile"
  description="How this site collects and uses anonymous analytics data, your rights, and how to contact the site owner."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-wrap">

      <header class="legal-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">
          Effective date: <time datetime="2026-08-18">18 August 2026</time> ·
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-08-18">18 August 2026</time>
        </p>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          This policy explains what data this site collects, why, and what rights you have.
          It is written in plain language — no legalese.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="controller">
        <h2 id="controller">1. Who is responsible for this site?</h2>
        <p>
          This site is operated by <strong>Kranthi Kumar Nagulapally</strong>, an independent
          professional. There is no company, employer, or organisation associated with this
          site's data processing. All enquiries about this policy should be directed to the
          contact address in Section 7.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="what-we-collect">
        <h2 id="what-we-collect">2. What data does this site collect?</h2>
        <p>
          This site collects <strong>anonymous, event-level click data</strong> when you
          interact with links or buttons. Specifically, each event record contains:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Action type</strong> — e.g. "link_click" or "button_click"</li>
          <li><strong>Label</strong> — the visible text of the element you clicked</li>
          <li><strong>Page path</strong> — the URL path where the click occurred (e.g. <code>/</code> or <code>/models/executive-portfolio/</code>)</li>
          <li><strong>Timestamp</strong> — the date and time of the event in ISO 8601 format</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>What is not collected:</strong> your name, email address, IP address,
          device fingerprint, persistent user ID, or any information that could identify
          you across visits or sessions. Each event is fully independent and unlinked
          to any other event.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site does <strong>not</strong> use cookies, local storage, or any form of
          tracking that persists between sessions. No advertising networks, social media
          pixels, or third-party analytics platforms (such as Google Analytics) are used.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="why">
        <h2 id="why">3. Why is this data collected?</h2>
        <p>
          The anonymous click data is used solely to understand which content on this site
          is most useful to visitors — for example, which frameworks or articles are read,
          and whether the contact or resume links are used. This information is used to
          improve the site's content and navigation.
        </p>
        <p>
          No data is used for advertising, profiling, automated decision-making, or any
          purpose other than the operational improvement of this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="legal-basis">
        <h2 id="legal-basis">4. Legal basis for processing (EU/UK GDPR)</h2>
        <p>
          The legal basis for collecting anonymous click data is <strong>Legitimate
          Interest</strong> under Article 6(1)(f) of the UK and EU GDPR. The interest is
          the operational maintenance and improvement of this website. Because the data
          collected contains no personal identifiers and cannot be linked to an individual,
          the privacy impact of this processing is minimal and proportionate.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are located in California (USA), this site does not sell or share personal
          information as defined under the CCPA, because no personal information is collected.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention">
        <h2 id="retention">5. How long is data retained?</h2>
        <p>
          Click events are transmitted as a one-way signal from your browser to this site's
          server-side endpoint at the time of interaction. No event data is stored in your
          browser after transmission.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the server side, events may be forwarded as a notification to an internal
          channel (such as a messaging application) for the site owner's review. This
          notification contains only the anonymous fields described in Section 2 and is
          subject to the retention policy of that channel. Events are not stored in any
          database or long-term log by this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="third-parties">
        <h2 id="third-parties">6. Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          This site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare's Workers platform</strong>. Cloudflare
          processes network traffic as a technical intermediary and may log connection
          metadata (such as IP addresses) at the network level as part of its standard
          operations. This is governed by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          No event data collected by this site is sold, licensed, or shared with any
          third-party advertiser, data broker, or analytics provider.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="rights">
        <h2 id="rights">7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the UK GDPR and EU GDPR, you have the following rights in relation to
          personal data. Because this site does not collect personal data (as defined
          by those laws), most of these rights have limited practical application here.
          However, you are entitled to exercise them:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right of access</strong> — request a copy of any personal data held about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — request deletion of any personal data.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to restrict processing</strong> — request that processing be limited while a dispute is resolved.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to lodge a complaint</strong> — if you are in the UK, you may contact the
            <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ICO (Information Commissioner's Office)</a>.
            If you are in the EU, contact your local supervisory authority.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact:
          <!-- TODO: Replace with your professional email after domain registration -->
          <strong><a href="mailto:nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com">nagulapalli.kranthi@gmail.com</a></strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Requests will be acknowledged within <strong>72 hours</strong> and resolved
          within <strong>30 days</strong> as required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes materially, the effective date above will be updated.
          Continued use of the site after a policy update constitutes acceptance of the
          updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 80px 8% 120px;
  }

  .legal-wrap {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 32px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  }

  .legal-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -1.5px;
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: 16px 0 14px;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    color: var(--brand-silver);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .legal-intro {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #cbd5e1;
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 44px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.5vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }

  p {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 12px 0 16px 24px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  li {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--brand-azure);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:hover {
    color: white;
  }

  code {
    font-family: "Consolas", "Courier New", monospace;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
